{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Hanging out with Friends"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Reminiscing About the Good Old Days"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "  Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le01ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Used to and Would"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> and  <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> have rather similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "However, there is an important difference between  <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and  <span class=\"strong\">would</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while  <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> does not require this. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the following examples: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We would visit India every summer when we were children. </span> <br> <span class=\"italic\">We used to visit India every summer. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I used to write down every single step of my favorite recipes!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We would try them out with my friends at school."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did you use to write down the recipes?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wouldn't show them to anyone!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Would you visit every India every summer?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Be careful of the question form of <span class=\"italic\">used to</span>. <br> Example: Did you <span class=\"strong\">use to</span> go to India every summer? "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Present Perfect vs.The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<ol><li>We use the Present Perfect tense for actions which started in the past and are still happening now OR for finished actions which have a connection to the present.</li><li>We use the Simple Past tense for past events or actions which have no connection to the present.</li></ol>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Rule\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect</span> is used when the time period has NOT finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Have you always kept a cooking diary?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The time period goes up to the present.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Past</span> is used when the time period HAS finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I was a picky eater as a kid </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I am not a picky eater anymore.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "engaging"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " captivating and appealing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to write an engaging piece about friendships."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le01ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in a conversation about childhood memories."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "interviewee "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who is interviewed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(nou